      text: "The statement “By walking the middle way, Buddhists avoid attachment to life” is reflected deeply in the significance of Temple Puja for the Buddhist community. Temple Puja provides a communal space where Buddhists practise the Middle Way together, balancing everyday responsibilities with spiritual reflection. By coming together regularly, the community learns to moderate desires, reminding themselves that, as the quote suggests, avoiding attachment is a shared goal rather than an individual struggle.\n\nDuring Temple Puja, offerings of candles, incense, and flowers symbolise the temporary nature of all things. These communal offerings help the community collectively recognise impermanence and let go of attachment. This joint practice reinforces the idea expressed in the quote — that Buddhists walk a balanced path by neither clinging to material life nor rejecting it entirely. Meditation and chanting performed as a group strengthen harmony and mutual support, making the Middle Way a lived communal experience. Thus, Temple Puja is significant because it binds the community through shared ethical values, modelling how a Buddhist society can function with restraint, mindfulness, and compassion.\n\nA key similarity between Theravada and Mahayana Buddhism is that both communities use Temple Puja to preserve the teachings of the Buddha and uphold the Middle Way. In both traditions, chanting, meditation, and offering rituals serve to reduce attachment and guide practitioners toward wisdom.\n\nHowever, a notable difference lies in the focus of the ritual. Theravada communities typically emphasise honouring the historical Buddha and cultivating personal discipline, using Puja to support individual insight and detachment. Mahayana communities, on the other hand, often incorporate bodhisattvas into Puja, using the ritual to express compassion and the vow to help all beings — another way of practising the principle in the quote: avoiding attachment not only to material things but also to one’s own self-interest.\n\nOverall, Temple Puja allows the community to embody the message of “walking the middle way” together, strengthening collective identity and spiritual purpose.",
